# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# Node / frontend dependencies and build outputs
node_modules
dist
gen/schemas

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Captured screenshots and anything derived from real capture output.
# The product brief makes this a hard constraint, not a preference: this repository is public, and a
# Capture may contain personal data. Nothing enforced it until 2026-08-23, when a UX audit staged five
# screenshots of the owner's own machine for commit and was caught by hand.
# Widened 2026-08-23 from `.work/**` to everywhere, after the CI guard's first run found twelve
# screenshots of the running product committed under _bmad-output/ since W1 — see BUG-7. The
# constraint was never about one directory.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
!apps/desktop/assets/app-icon.png
!apps/desktop/assets/app-icon.ico

# Raw accessibility-tree dumps from UI audit workers. They are JSON snapshots of the RUNNING
# product and they embed absolute paths under the operator's home directory, so they fall under the
# same brief constraint as a screenshot: derived from real capture output, and this repo is public.
# The distilled AUDIT*.md files are what survives an audit; the raw dumps are scratch.
.work/**/tree-*.txt
